is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I verified router11’s OSPF and routing state and found it healthy and able to reach the Campus 2 SVI. Router11 has Full adjacencies to both neighbors (show ip ospf neighbor: 192.168.10.2 on 10.1.1.0/24 and 192.168.144.2 on 10.1.0.0/24). Its OSPF routes include 10.5.0.0/24 installed via 10.1.0.2 on eth0. A direct test from router11 to the Campus 2 SVI succeeds (ping 10.5.0.254: 0% loss; traceroute shows 10.1.0.2 -> 10.5.0.254). Other “external” prefixes are present as well (e.g., 55.5.1.0/24, 172.25.1.0/24), and Linux forwarding/rp_filter/firewall settings are normal.

Localization and comparison: router11 is a “dual-homed” spoke (OSPF on 10.1.0.0/24 to router17 and on 10.1.1.0/24 to router1), which yields ECMP entries (e.g., 10.0.0.0/24 via 10.1.0.2 and 10.1.1.1). Router10 and router8 show analogous healthy OSPF states and likewise can reach 10.5.0.254. Attempts to ping 8.8.8.8 fail from all spokes with ICMP Host Unreachable from 55.5.1.2 (the upstream), so that behavior is not unique to router11.

Root cause: No misconfiguration found on router11; current evidence shows proper OSPF operation and reachability to 10.5.0.254. 

Corrective fix: None required. If the earlier symptom recurs, focus on the 10.1.0.0/24 adjacency to router17 (10.1.0.2), because loss of that neighbor would remove the 10.5.0.0/24 route from router11. At present, the route and adjacency are up and functioning. 
=== END ===